# Mobile `@/modules` Structure

Feature UI lives under **`apps/mobile/src/modules/<domain>/`**. Next.js `app/` routes stay thin and only wire data → screen.

| Folder | Purpose | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `screens/` | Full page compositions used by route files | `DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen` |
| `sections/` | Page sections composed by screens (split large sections into sibling folders) | `DiscoveryClubsDetailHeroSection`, `…HeroSectionLightbox`, `…PullToView`, `…Header` |
| `lib/` | Domain helpers / demo data for that module | `club-detail-data.ts` |

## Per-component folder shape

Screens and sections use a **PascalCase folder** with:

```
packages path example:
modules/discovery/screens/DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen/
  DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen.tsx
  DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen.styles.ts
  DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen.types.ts
  index.ts
```

## Rules

1. **Route files stay thin** — `app/**/page.tsx` loads data and renders a module screen; no large UI inline.
2. **One screen/section per folder** — folder name matches the component name.
3. **Naming** — `<Domain><Feature><Screen|…Section>` (e.g. `DiscoveryClubsDetailScreen`, `DiscoveryClubsDetailHeroSection`).
4. **Import path** — `@/modules/<domain>/screens/<Name>` or `@/modules/<domain>/sections/<Name>`.
5. **Primitives** — build with `@heroui/react` + `@repo/icons`; shared composites from `@repo/ui`.
6. **Images** — use `next/image` (or `@repo/ui` `MediaImage`); never raw `<img>`.
